# ─── GitHub Control Hub CLI ───
#
# No .env file is needed in most cases.
#
# FIRST-TIME SETUP (CLI-only, no web app):
#   1. Make sure you have valid AWS credentials (aws sso login)
#   2. Run: ghch setup
#      This creates DynamoDB tables, the Secrets Manager secret,
#      and saves your org config locally (~/.ghch/config.json).
#   3. Run: ghch login
#
# USING ALONGSIDE THE WEB APP:
#   If you already have the web app deployed (CloudFormation stack),
#   just run 'ghch login'. Tables, secrets, and org are auto-resolved
#   from the existing stack.
#
# Override these ONLY if your naming differs from the defaults:
# STACK_NAME=github-control-hub
# SECRET_NAME=github-control-hub/secrets
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1
